                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">memorandum relative to petitions to be presented to
                        the ministry of fomento of the de facto government of mexico for extension
                        of time for operation of mines</hi>
                </head>
                <p>The Ministry of Fomento, in response to various requests presented by the
                    American Embassy on behalf of American citizens for an extension of time in
                    which to resume or begin the operation of mining properties, has indicated that
                    the interested parties must make their petitions directly to the Ministry.</p>
                <p>Such petitions must be written in the Spanish language, bear a properly canceled
                    fifty centavo Mexican documentary stamp, be signed by the owner of the property
                    in question or his legal representative, and set forth the following points: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>The name, title number, exact location, and number of pertenencias
                            (area) of the mining property for which extension of time is
                            required.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>The reasons which the owner alleges for the nonoperation of his
                            property.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>A request that extension of time be granted in which to begin or
                            resume operation.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>This petition should be accompanied by the last boleta or mining tax receipt, in
                    order to show that the taxes are paid up to date.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-10"><hi rendition="#italic">March 10,
                                1917</hi></date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
